<h4 class="dialog-section-title">Important Information About Belt Examinations</h4>
<ul class="dialog-list">
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Belt examinations are not mandatory; participation requires the mutual consent of both the instructor and the student.</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Candidates first demonstrate foundational movements, followed by formal exercises (kata).</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> At advanced levels, the examination incorporates complex partner techniques, knife defenses, and board breaking.</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Examinations for colored belts can be undertaken on a semiannual basis.</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Younger practitioners initially test for supplementary colored stripes on their belts rather than full colored belts.</li>
</ul>

<div class="dialog-cta-note">
	<strong>Important:</strong> Your safety is strictly guaranteed during all belt examinations. Furthermore, your progression is entirely self-paced:
	you only need to test when you feel fully prepared and confident to do so.
</div>